my $CODE = <<'END_CODE';
hello world
END_CODE

{
    desc => q{u undoes replace mode changes},
    description => <<'END_DESC',
## Macro: `xt/visual/macros/undo_after_replace`

Tests that **u** restores text that was overwritten in replace mode (**R**).
The entire insert session in replace mode is treated as one undo unit.

**Keys:** `R`, type `XXXX`, `Escape`, `u`

**initial.png**
- Buffer contains "hello world"
- Cursor at column 0 on 'h'

**after_replace.png**
- Buffer contains "XXXXo world" (first 4 chars replaced with X)
- Intermediate snapshot showing the replacement

**after_undo.png**
- Buffer restored to "hello world" (identical to initial)
- Entire replace session undone as one unit
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('RXXXX');
        $ctx->key('Escape');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_replace');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('u');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_undo');
    },
}
